body:
Wouldn't usually the default Variant hash take care of hashing in projects, leaving this buggy code untouched?
Tested it with this, turns out it doesn't use `Color::hash()` (if it was we would have seen fallout from this bug sooner, since with this function changes in `g` don't affect the hash)
```gdscript
@tool
extends EditorScript

func _run() -> void:
    var color_1: Color = Color(1, 0, 0)
    var color_2: Color = Color(1, 1, 0)

    print("color 1: ", color_1, " hash: ", hash(color_1))
    print("color 2: ", color_2, " hash: ", hash(color_2))
```

I also searched for any calls of `Color::hash()` in the codebase but couldn't find any (and even if, it would only be a problem if some hashes were hard coded there, (_a problem in terms of breaking change_)). There is the possibility that I missed some, especially if there happen to be any HashMaps that use Colors as keys, but those hashes would be refreshed when compiling and can't cause any breaking issues. 

So you maybe could call fixing this bug "breaking" technically, but there is nothing for it to break, so it's fine i think.
